{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_flat`, a deterministic row-major reshape of the original observed `y` with `y_flat[(j - 1) * n_trials + t] = y[j, t]`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `y_flat` to `data_safe.json` using that deterministic flattening. The original `y` is retained as context for the lagged history calculations, so the protected variable is not read before its single observation. Replaced the nested cellwise Bernoulli sampling statements with one vectorized `y_flat ~ bernoulli(p_safestan)`. Replaced the two indexed beta priors with one vectorized top-level prior `beta ~ uniform(beta_lower, beta_upper)`. These are mechanical same-density rewrites for the supplied data; no new non-deterministic data values were introduced.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> n_trials;
  int<lower=0> n_dogs;
  array[n_dogs, n_trials] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
  array[n_dogs * n_trials] int<lower=0, upper=1> y_flat;
}
transformed data {
  vector[2] beta_lower;
  vector[2] beta_upper;

  beta_lower[1] = -100;
  beta_lower[2] = 0;
  beta_upper[1] = 0;
  beta_upper[2] = 100;
}
parameters {
  vector[2] beta;
}
transformed parameters {
  matrix[n_dogs, n_trials] n_avoid;
  matrix[n_dogs, n_trials] n_shock;
  matrix[n_dogs, n_trials] p;
  array[n_dogs * n_trials] real p_safestan;

  for (j in 1 : n_dogs) {
    n_avoid[j, 1] = 0;
    n_shock[j, 1] = 0;
    for (t in 2 : n_trials) {
      n_avoid[j, t] = n_avoid[j, t - 1] + 1 - y[j, t - 1];
      n_shock[j, t] = n_shock[j, t - 1] + y[j, t - 1];
    }
    for (t in 1 : n_trials) {
      p[j, t] = inv_logit(beta[1] * n_avoid[j, t] + beta[2] * n_shock[j, t]);
      p_safestan[(j - 1) * n_trials + t] = p[j, t];
    }
  }
}
model {
  beta ~ uniform(beta_lower, beta_upper);
  y_flat ~ bernoulli(p_safestan);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"n_dogs":2,"n_trials":3,"y":[[1,0,0],[0,1,0]],"y_flat":[1,0,0,0,1,0]}","protected_variables":["y_flat"]}
